Store the outer radius and the padding in custom properties and derive the inner radius with `calc()`. Changing either value then updates the inner corners automatically, using inner = outer − padding.

```css
.outer {
  --outer-radius: 24px;
  --padding: 8px;
  --inner-radius: calc(var(--outer-radius) - var(--padding));

  border-radius: var(--outer-radius);
  padding: var(--padding);
}

.inner {
  border-radius: var(--inner-radius);   /* 24px − 8px = 16px */
}
```

To start from the inner radius instead, compute `--outer-radius: calc(var(--inner-radius) + var(--padding))`. This relies on custom properties inheriting from `.outer` to `.inner`. If padding differs per side or there is a border, add those to the calculation.

