Walk the array once and **collect each index** where the element matches, for example with `reduce()` and an array accumulator.

```js
const indexOfAll = (arr, val) =>
  arr.reduce((acc, el, i) => {
    if (el === val) acc.push(i);
    return acc;
  }, []);

indexOfAll([1, 2, 3, 1, 2, 3], 1); // [0, 3]
indexOfAll([1, 2, 3], 4); // []
```

An empty array (not `-1`) means "no matches", so callers can loop over the result without a special case.

