```js
const names = ['Ana', 'Ben', 'Cy'];
new Intl.ListFormat('en-US').format(names);   // 'Ana, Ben, and Cy'
new Intl.ListFormat('en-GB').format(names);   // 'Ana, Ben and Cy'
new Intl.ListFormat('en-US', { type: 'disjunction' }).format(names);
// 'Ana, Ben, or Cy'
new Intl.ListFormat('en-US', { style: 'short' }).format(names);
// 'Ana, Ben, & Cy'
```

`type` is `'conjunction'` (and, default), `'disjunction'` (or) or `'unit'`; `style` is `'long'` (default), `'short'` or `'narrow'`. Two items give `'Ana and Ben'` with no comma. Create the formatter once and reuse it when formatting many lists.

