Static fields are inherited: `Post.instances` looks up the prototype chain and finds `Model.instances`, so every subclass pushes into the same array. Fix it by keeping a registry keyed by class name and having each subclass register itself in a `static { }` block, which runs once when the class is defined, with `this` set to that class.

```js
class Model {
  static instances = []; // shared by ALL subclasses
}
class Post extends Model {}
class Author extends Model {}
Post.instances === Author.instances; // true

// Fix: one bucket per subclass
class Model2 {
  static registry = {};
  static prepare(model) { Model2.registry[model.name] ??= []; }
}
class Comment extends Model2 {
  static { Model2.prepare(this); } // this === Comment
}
```

Static initialization blocks are standard since ES2022 and work in all current browsers and Node.

