It merges with `Object.assign({}, base, ...traitObjects)`. Later arguments overwrite earlier ones, so traits override the base, and a later trait overrides an earlier one.

```js
static build(...desiredTraits) {
  const { model, base, traits } = Factory.factoryMap.get(this.name);
  const data = Object.assign(
    {},                                     // fresh object: base is not mutated
    base,
    ...desiredTraits.map(name => traits[name])
  );
  return new model(data);
}

PostFactory.build();
// Post { id: 1, title: 'Post title', publishedAt: null }
PostFactory.build('published');
// Post { id: 1, title: 'Post title', publishedAt: 2025-01-02T00:00:00.000Z }
```

Pitfalls: the merge is shallow, so nested objects are shared between built objects; and a misspelled trait name maps to `undefined`, which `Object.assign` silently ignores.

