Use `Object.fromEntries(map)`. It accepts any iterable of `[key, value]` pairs, and a `Map` iterates as exactly that, so `.entries()` is optional.

```js
const mapToObject = map => Object.fromEntries(map);

mapToObject(new Map([['a', 1], ['b', 2]])); // { a: 1, b: 2 }

mapToObject(new Map([[2, 'b'], [{}, 1]]));
// { '2': 'b', '[object Object]': 1 }
```

Object keys can only be strings or symbols, so other keys are converted to strings, and two different object keys would collide on `'[object Object]'`. Convert before sending a `Map` in JSON: `JSON.stringify(map)` gives `'{}'`.

