back:
Pass the form element to `new FormData(form)` and convert it with `Object.fromEntries(...)`. Keys are the fields' `name` attributes.

```js
form.addEventListener('submit', event => {
  event.preventDefault();
  const data = Object.fromEntries(new FormData(event.currentTarget));
  // { email: 'test@email.com', name: 'Test Name' }
});
```

Fields that submit several values under one name (checkbox groups, `<select multiple>`) keep only the last value. Read those with `formData.getAll('topics')`. Values are always strings (or `File` objects), so convert numbers and booleans yourself, and unchecked checkboxes are missing entirely.

