back:
In sloppy (non-strict) mode, `this` is the global object (`globalThis`, which is `window` in a browser). In strict mode it is `undefined`.

```js
function sloppy() { return this; }
sloppy() === globalThis; // true (in a non-module script)

function strict() {
  'use strict';
  return this;
}
strict(); // undefined
```

ES modules (`import`/`export`) and `class` bodies are always strict, so in modern code a detached call gives `undefined`. That is why `const save = form.save; save();` fails with "Cannot read properties of undefined" instead of quietly reading globals. Fix it with `form.save.bind(form)` or an arrow wrapper: `() => form.save()`.

