Anchor the pattern and validate each segment: day `0?[1-9]|[12]\d|3[01]`, month `0?[1-9]|1[0-2]`, year `\d{4}`. But a regex only checks the *shape*: it happily accepts `31/02/2024`, so you still need to check the real calendar date.

```js
const ddmmyyyy = /^(0?[1-9]|[12]\d|3[01])([\/-])(0?[1-9]|1[0-2])\2\d{4}$/;
ddmmyyyy.test('15/03/2024'); // true
ddmmyyyy.test('15/03-2024'); // false (\2 forces the same separator)
ddmmyyyy.test('31/02/2024'); // true  (shape OK, date impossible)

const isRealDate = s => {
  const [d, m, y] = s.split(/[\/-]/).map(Number);
  const dt = new Date(y, m - 1, d);
  return dt.getDate() === d && dt.getMonth() === m - 1;
};
isRealDate('31/02/2024'); // false (Date rolled over to March)
```

