Use rest parameters to gather separate arguments into an array (`toVariadic`), and use spread to expand an array into separate arguments (`fromVariadic`). "Variadic" means the function accepts any number of arguments.

```js
const toVariadic = fn => (...args) => fn(args);
const fromVariadic = fn => args => fn(...args);

const allPromises = toVariadic(Promise.all.bind(Promise));
allPromises(Promise.resolve(1), Promise.resolve(2)).then(console.log);
// [1, 2]

const arrayMax = fromVariadic(Math.max);
arrayMax([1, 2, 3]); // 3
```

Day to day you'd just write `Math.max(...values)` inline. Beware that spreading a very large array (hundreds of thousands of items) can exceed the engine's argument limit.

