Use a `function*` with an endless `while (true)` loop. Each pass yields `arr[i % arr.length]` and then increments `i`. The modulo operator `%` wraps the index back to 0 after the last element.

```js
const cycle = function* (arr) {
  let i = 0;
  while (true) {
    yield arr[i % arr.length];
    i++;
  }
};

const colors = cycle(['red', 'green', 'blue']);
colors.next().value; // 'red'
colors.next().value; // 'green'
colors.next().value; // 'blue'
colors.next().value; // 'red'
```

An infinite loop is safe here because a generator pauses at each `yield` until you call `next()`. Never spread an infinite generator (`[...cycle(x)]`): that never finishes.

