Walk the seven days in order, look up each day's hours (defaulting to `'Closed'`), and either **extend the current run** if the hours match the previous day or **start a new run**. Filling missing days and grouping happen in the same loop; then format each run.

```js
const DAYS = ['Monday', 'Tuesday', 'Wednesday', 'Thursday', 'Friday', 'Saturday', 'Sunday'];

const formatOpeningHours = input => {
  const hoursByDay = new Map(input.map(({ day, from, to }) => [day, `${from} - ${to}`]));
  const groups = [];
  for (const day of DAYS) {
    const hours = hoursByDay.get(day) ?? 'Closed';
    const last = groups.at(-1);
    if (last?.hours === hours) last.end = day; // extend the run
    else groups.push({ start: day, end: day, hours });
  }
  return groups.map(({ start, end, hours }) =>
    `${start === end ? start : `${start} - ${end}`}: ${hours}`);
};
```

Keying the `Map` by day avoids searching the array for every day. Consecutive closed days group too (`'Saturday - Sunday: Closed'`).

