Check whether the scroll position plus the visible height reaches the full page height: `window.scrollY + documentElement.clientHeight >= documentElement.scrollHeight`. The modern approach is an `IntersectionObserver` watching a "sentinel" element placed after the list.

```js
const bottomVisible = () => {
  const { scrollHeight, clientHeight } = document.documentElement;
  return window.scrollY + clientHeight >= scrollHeight - 1; // 1px for rounding
};

// Modern: get notified when the sentinel scrolls into view
const sentinel = document.querySelector('#load-more-sentinel');
new IntersectionObserver(([entry]) => {
  if (entry.isIntersecting) loadNextPage();
}).observe(sentinel);
```

`scrollY` can be fractional on zoomed or high-DPI screens, so an exact `===` check may never be true. Calling `bottomVisible()` from a `scroll` handler runs on every scroll event; `IntersectionObserver` avoids that work and fires only when visibility changes.

