Call `navigator.clipboard.writeText(text)`, which returns a promise. It needs a **secure context** (HTTPS or `localhost`) and, in practice, a **user action**, so call it from a click handler and handle rejection.

```js
copyBtn.addEventListener('click', async () => {
  try {
    await navigator.clipboard.writeText(shareLink.value);
    status.textContent = 'Link copied'; // status has aria-live="polite"
  } catch {
    status.textContent = 'Copy failed: select the link and copy it manually';
  }
});
```

On plain HTTP `navigator.clipboard` is `undefined`, so the call throws. Always give visible feedback; an `aria-live` region also announces it to screen-reader users. The old `document.execCommand('copy')` trick is deprecated.

