The listener is **never removed**: it keeps running (and returning early) on every later event and keeps its closure in memory. Fix it by having the listener remove itself, or just use `{ once: true }`.

```js
// Flag: still attached forever
let fired = false;
btn.addEventListener('click', e => {
  if (fired) return;
  fired = true;
  handle(e);
});

// Self-removing
const handleOnce = e => {
  btn.removeEventListener('click', handleOnce);
  handle(e);
};
btn.addEventListener('click', handleOnce);

// Best today
btn.addEventListener('click', handle, { once: true });
```

The self-removing version needs a named function, because `removeEventListener()` needs the same function reference.

