Make each widget a self-contained ES module and load it with dynamic `import()` only when its element is on the page. The bundle for page A then never includes widget B's code or its libraries.

```js
// main.mjs (loaded with <script type="module">)
if (document.querySelector('math-formula')) {
  await import('/components/math-formula.mjs'); // defines <math-formula>
}
```

Self-contained means each module registers its own element and brings its own styles, with no shared globals, so modules load in any order. Bundlers (Vite, webpack) turn each dynamic `import()` into a separate chunk automatically. Same idea as `React.lazy` for routes.

