Use **`typeof value === 'function'`**. It is `true` for every callable: regular, arrow, async and generator functions, and classes.

```js
const isFunction = val => typeof val === 'function';

function save(data, onSuccess) {
  // ...save data...
  if (isFunction(onSuccess)) onSuccess(data);
}

isFunction(x => x); // true
isFunction('x'); // false
```

Pitfall: optional call `onSuccess?.(data)` only skips when `onSuccess` is `null` or `undefined`. If someone passes a string or an object, it still throws `TypeError: onSuccess is not a function`. Also, classes pass the check but throw if called without `new`. To check whether a value is an *instance* of a class, use `instanceof`.

