Use **`as` in an export list**: `export { internalName as publicName };`. Importers must then use the public name.

```js
// auth.js
const key = 'dev-only-key';
const verifyToken = token => token === key;

export { key as authKey, verifyToken as verify };
export { verifyToken as default }; // can also become the default export

// index.js
import { authKey, verify } from './auth.js';
```

This lets you keep short or descriptive names inside the file while exposing a clearer API, or keep an old public name working after renaming the internal function. Real secrets should come from environment variables (`process.env.AUTH_KEY`), not from source code.

