Rename at least one with **`as` in the import**: `import { format as formatDate } from './dates.js';`. The name before `as` must match the export; the name after it is the local variable you use.

```js
// dates.js exports format(date); money.js exports format(amount)
import { format as formatDate } from './dates.js';
import { format as formatMoney } from './money.js';

formatDate(new Date());
formatMoney(19.99);
```

Renaming only affects your file; the exporting module is unchanged. An alternative is a namespace import: `import * as dates from './dates.js'` and then `dates.format(...)`.

