Strip the `#`, expand 3- or 4-digit shorthand by doubling each digit, then read each **pair of hex digits** with `parseInt(pair, 16)`: the pairs are red, green, blue and an optional alpha. The alpha must be **divided by 255**, because CSS `rgba()` expects alpha from 0 to 1.

```js
const hexToRgb = hex => {
  let h = hex.replace(/^#/, '');
  if (h.length === 3 || h.length === 4) h = [...h].map(c => c + c).join('');
  const [r, g, b, a] = h.match(/../g).map(pair => parseInt(pair, 16));
  return a === undefined
    ? `rgb(${r}, ${g}, ${b})`
    : `rgba(${r}, ${g}, ${b}, ${Number((a / 255).toFixed(3))})`;
};

