hexToRgb('#fff'); // 'rgb(255, 255, 255)'
hexToRgb('#27ae6080'); // 'rgba(39, 174, 96, 0.502)'
```

An alternative parses the whole number once and extracts channels with bit operations: `n >> 16 & 255` is red, `n >> 8 & 255` is green, `n & 255` is blue. Validate user-entered colors first (`/^#?([0-9a-f]{3,4}|[0-9a-f]{6}|[0-9a-f]{8})$/i`), because `parseInt` quietly returns `NaN` for bad input.

