Accept an options object and destructure it in the parameter list, with defaults. Every setting is then named at the call site, order no longer matters, and callers pass only what they need.

```js
const fetchUsers = ({ page = 1, pageSize = 20, includeInactive = false } = {}) =>
  `/api/users?page=${page}&size=${pageSize}&inactive=${includeInactive}`;

fetchUsers({ page: 2, includeInactive: true });
// '/api/users?page=2&size=20&inactive=true'
fetchUsers();
// '/api/users?page=1&size=20&inactive=false'

// Compare: fetchUsers(2, 20, true) (what is true?)
```

Keep the `= {}` after the pattern: without it, `fetchUsers()` throws a `TypeError` (`Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'page')`), because there is no object to destructure.

