back:
A silent fail is an error that is caught but then ignored: no log, no rethrow, no message to the user. The program continues as if nothing happened, so the real cause is lost and the bug shows up later somewhere unrelated (empty lists, `undefined` data), which makes it very hard to debug.

```js
// Silent: a failed request just leaves the page empty
fetch('/api/orders')
  .then(res => res.json())
  .then(renderOrders)
  .catch(() => {});

// Also silent
try {
  saveDraft(form);
} catch (err) {
  // nothing here
}
```

Fix: at least `console.error` the error and either rethrow it or show an error state. If ignoring an error really is correct (e.g. optional analytics), say so in a comment so the next reader knows it's deliberate.

