back:
Scale it with a transform (`transform: scale(1.1)` or the standalone `scale: 1.1`) and transition that property. Transforms only change how the element is painted, not its layout box, so neighboring elements do not move.

```css
.button-grow {
  transition: transform 0.3s ease-in-out;
}

.button-grow:hover,
.button-grow:focus-visible {
  transform: scale(1.1);
}
```

The individual `scale` property (`scale: 1.1` or `scale: 110%`) works in all modern browsers. It does not replace any `transform` already on the element (they combine), so use `transition: scale 0.3s` with it. Changing `width`/`padding` instead would push neighbors around and force layout on every frame.

