Shrinking pulls the button's edge out from under the pointer. Hover ends, the button grows back under the pointer, hover starts again, and the loop repeats as flicker. Keep the shrink small (e.g. `0.95`, a common "pressed" effect on `:active`), or put `:hover` on a wrapper that does not change size and scale the inner element.

```css
.button-shrink {
  transition: transform 0.2s ease-in-out;
}

/* Subtle press feedback */
.button-shrink:active {
  transform: scale(0.95);   /* or: scale: 95%; */
}

/* Or: hover the stable wrapper, shrink the child */
.wrap:hover > .button-shrink {
  transform: scale(0.8);
}
```

Hit-testing follows the transformed shape, so a scaled-down element has a smaller hover area. That is also true for grow effects, but there the area only gets bigger.

