To create a **two-sided card** that rotates on hover, you first need a container element with two child elements, one for the front side and one for the back side of the card. You can then use the `rotateY()` function to rotate the card around the Y-axis, and the `backface-visibility` property to hide the back side of the card when it is not visible.

```html
<div class="rotating-card">
  <div class="card-side front"></div>
  <div class="card-side back"></div>
</div>
```

```css
.rotating-card {
  perspective: 150rem;
  position: relative;
  box-shadow: none;
  background: none;
}

.rotating-card .card-side {
  transition: all 0.8s ease;
  backface-visibility: hidden;
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
}

.rotating-card .card-side.back {
  transform: rotateY(-180deg);
}

.rotating-card:hover .card-side.front {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

.rotating-card:hover .card-side.back {
  transform: rotateY(0deg);
}
```

---
Adapted from [30 seconds of code](https://github.com/30-seconds/30-seconds-of-code/blob/f1b2d5a65c32432a877de94a749be40a396ebed2/content/snippets/css/s/card-hover-effects.md) · [CC BY 4.0](/licenses/30-seconds.txt).

back:
Stack both faces on top of each other, pre-rotate the back face by 180° with `rotateY`, and set `backface-visibility: hidden` on both faces so each one disappears when turned away. Set `perspective` on the container for depth. On hover, rotate the front to 180° and the back to 0°.

```css
.flip-card { perspective: 150rem; position: relative; }

.flip-card .side {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  backface-visibility: hidden;
  transition: transform 0.8s ease;
}

.flip-card .back { transform: rotateY(-180deg); }

.flip-card:is(:hover, :focus-within) .front { transform: rotateY(180deg); }
.flip-card:is(:hover, :focus-within) .back  { transform: rotateY(0deg); }
```

Hover-only content is unreachable on touch screens and by keyboard. Adding `:focus-within` (or toggling a class on click) lets everyone reach the back. Because both faces are absolutely positioned, the container needs an explicit height.

