back:
It makes the elements behave like a table and a cell, and `vertical-align: middle` (plus `text-align: center`) centers content inside a table cell. It is a legacy workaround from before flexbox. Replace it with `display: grid; place-items: center` or flexbox.

```css
/* Legacy */
.table-centering { display: table; width: 100%; height: 100%; }
.table-centering > .content {
  display: table-cell;
  text-align: center;
  vertical-align: middle;
}

/* Modern replacement */
.centered { display: grid; place-items: center; }
```

The parent needs an actual height (for example `height: 100%` inside a sized ancestor) for vertical centering to be visible. Table display also brings table sizing quirks. Recognize it when maintaining old code, but don't write it for new code.

---
Adapted from [30 seconds of code](https://github.com/30-seconds/30-seconds-of-code/blob/f1b2d5a65c32432a877de94a749be40a396ebed2/content/snippets/css/s/centering.md) · [CC BY 4.0](/licenses/30-seconds.txt).

