Adapted from [30 seconds of code](https://github.com/30-seconds/30-seconds-of-code/blob/f1b2d5a65c32432a877de94a749be40a396ebed2/content/snippets/css/s/footer-at-the-bottom.md) · [CC BY 4.0](/licenses/30-seconds.txt).

back:
Give `body` `display: grid`, a minimum height of the full viewport, and a row template where the content row is `1fr` and the footer row is `auto`. The `1fr` row takes all the leftover height, so the footer sits at the bottom on short pages and follows the content on long pages.

```css
body {
  margin: 0;
  min-height: 100vh;   /* fallback */
  min-height: 100dvh;  /* dynamic viewport: correct with mobile browser bars */
  display: grid;
  grid-template-rows: 1fr auto;   /* main, footer */
}
```

The row list must match `body`'s direct children. With a header it becomes `auto 1fr auto`, and an extra wrapper or stray element shifts everything down a row. `dvh` accounts for mobile address bars that grow and shrink; `100vh` can be taller than the visible area on phones.

