If you want an element to **fill its parent container**, you can simply use `inset: 0` to set all sides to `0`. This is a concise way to set `top`, `right`, `bottom`, and `left` to `0`.

```html
<div class="parent">
  <div class="child"></div>
</div>
```

```css
.parent {
  position: relative;
}

.child {
  position: absolute;
  /* Fill the parent */
  /* top: 0, right: 0, bottom: 0, left: 0 */
  inset: 0;
}
```

