`z-index: 0` on a positioned element creates a new stacking context. The `::before`'s `z-index: -1` then puts it behind the link's text but still inside the link. Without the stacking context, `-1` would push the pseudo-element behind the link's ancestors, such as a nav background, and the highlight would vanish.

```css
nav a {
  position: relative;
  z-index: 0;              /* new stacking context */
  display: block;
}

nav a::before {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  z-index: -1;             /* behind the text, inside the link */
  background: #2683f6;
  transform: scale(0);
  transition: transform 0.5s ease-in-out;
}

nav a:is(:hover, :focus-visible)::before { transform: scale(1); }
```

`:focus-visible` shows the effect for keyboard focus without it sticking after a mouse click. Check that the text color still has enough contrast on the blue background.

