back:
On the container, set `overflow-y: auto`, `scroll-snap-type: y mandatory`, and a limited height; on each section, set `scroll-snap-align: start`. Without a fixed or maximum height, the container just grows with its content and never scrolls.

```css
.vertical-snap {
  height: 100dvh;                   /* or max-height */
  overflow-y: auto;
  scroll-snap-type: y mandatory;
  overscroll-behavior-y: contain;   /* no pull-to-refresh / page chaining */
}

.vertical-snap > section {
  scroll-snap-align: start;
}
```

Use `mandatory` only when every section fits in the viewport. Taller sections are awkward to read under mandatory snapping (browsers let you scroll inside them, but snapping keeps interfering), so `proximity` is safer for them.

