Components only use variables (`background: var(--bg)`). A theme is just a different set of variable values: define the defaults on `:root`, then redefine the same names under a `.dark` class (for a manual toggle) or inside `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)` (to follow the OS). Because custom properties inherit, every element picks up the new values without changing any component CSS.

```css
:root {
  --bg: #fff;
  --text: #111;
  --muted: #555;
  color-scheme: light dark;   /* native controls & scrollbars follow too */
}

@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root { --bg: #111; --text: #eee; --muted: #aaa; }
}

:root.dark { --bg: #111; --text: #eee; --muted: #aaa; }

body  { background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); }
small { color: var(--muted); }
```

Check contrast in both themes. The newer `light-dark(#fff, #111)` function can pick between two values based on `color-scheme` in a single declaration.

