back:
Return a cleanup function from an effect with an empty dependency array; React calls it when the component unmounts. Because the effect ran only once, that cleanup closes over the `onUnmount` from the **first render**, so it sees first-render props and state. Keep the latest callback in a ref if it needs current values.

```jsx
function useUnmount(onUnmount) {
  const latest = useRef(onUnmount);
  useEffect(() => {
    latest.current = onUnmount;       // updated after every render
  });
  useEffect(() => () => latest.current(), []);
}

function Editor({ draft }) {
  useUnmount(() => saveDraft(draft));  // saves the latest draft, not the first
  return <textarea defaultValue={draft} />;
}
```

In development, StrictMode calls the cleanup once right after mount (then sets up again), so unmount code must be safe to run more than once.

