  return (
    <textarea
      value={value}
      onChange={e => onChange(e.target.value)}
      {...rest}
    />
  );
}

function CommentForm() {
  const [comment, setComment] = useState('');
  return <TextArea value={comment} onChange={setComment} rows={3} />;
}
```

Rule: a piece of state should live in exactly one place. If the parent owns it, the child just displays it. Passing `value` without `onChange` makes the field read-only (React warns about this).

