Animate `transform: scale()` to grow the circle and `opacity` to fade it, both in a `@keyframes` rule. `forwards` keeps the styles of the **last** keyframe after the animation ends; without it the circle would snap back to full opacity and small size for a moment.

```css
.ripple {
  animation: ripple-effect 0.9s ease forwards;
}

@keyframes ripple-effect {
  from { transform: scale(1);  opacity: 1; }
  to   { transform: scale(35); opacity: 0; }
}

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .ripple { animation: none; opacity: 0; }
}
```

`transform` and `opacity` are cheap to animate because they don't trigger layout, so the effect stays smooth on phones. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` for users who turn animations off.

