A state update happened **after** the test stopped waiting, typically from a promise, timer, or fetch that resolved later, so your assertions ran before the UI settled. Fix it by awaiting the change the user would see, using `findBy*` queries or `waitFor`, not by wrapping code in `act` yourself.

```jsx
test('shows a confirmation after saving', async () => {
  const user = userEvent.setup();
  render(<SaveButton />);

  await user.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /save/i }));

  // findBy* retries until the text appears (or times out)
  expect(await screen.findByText('Saved')).toBeInTheDocument();
});
```

Testing Library's `render`, `fireEvent`, and `userEvent` already wrap their work in `act`. If you do need `act` directly, React 19 exports it from `react` (`import { act } from 'react'`); the `react-dom/test-utils` version is deprecated (its other helpers were removed).

