`addEventListener` returns `undefined`, so `listener.current` is `undefined` and `removeEventListener('resize', undefined)` removes nothing. Every time `callback` changes, another listener is added and none are ever removed. Remove **the same function you added**, in the effect's cleanup.

```jsx
function useOnWindowResize(callback) {
  const latest = useRef(callback);
  useEffect(() => {
    latest.current = callback;
  });

  useEffect(() => {
    const handler = () => latest.current();
    window.addEventListener('resize', handler);
    return () => window.removeEventListener('resize', handler);
  }, []);
}

// useOnWindowResize(() => setIsMobile(window.innerWidth < 640));
```

The latest-ref keeps the listener attached once while still calling the newest callback, so an inline arrow function from the caller doesn't cause re-subscribing. `resize` fires many times during a drag; throttle or debounce expensive work.

